 MEMBERS ARE WORKING.'}{'symbol': 'CLX', 'date': '2019-10-31 08:30:00', 'title': 'CLOROX REPORTS Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.59', 'text': 'CLOROX REPORTS Q1 FISCAL YEAR 2020 RESULTS, CONFIRMS SALES AND EPS OUTLOOK.REAFFIRMS FY 2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $6.05 TO $6.25.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.59.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.54 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FIRST-QUARTER RESULTS WERE GENERALLY IN LINE WITH OUR EXPECTATIONS.REMAIN ON TRACK TO DELIVER OUR FISCAL YEAR OUTLOOK.QTRLY NET SALES $1.51 BILLION VERSUS $1.56 BILLION.QTRLY DILUTED EPS RESULTS WERE DUE PRIMARILY TO HIGHER TRADE PROMOTION SPENDING.'}{'symbol': 'CL', 'date': '2019-10-31 22:30:00', 'title': 'COLGATE-PALMOLIVE COMPANY PROVIDES EARNINGS GUIDANCE FOR THE YEAR 2019', 'text': 'COLGATE-PALMOLIVE COMPANY PROVIDED EARNINGS GUIDANCE FOR THE YEAR 2019. FOR THE PERIOD, THE COMPANY EXPECTS 2019 NET SALES TO BE FLAT TO UP LOW-SINGLE-DIGITS, WITH ORGANIC SALES NOW EXPECTED TO BE UP BETWEEN 3% AND 4%, ROUGHLY IN LINE WITH YEAR-TO-DATE GROWTH. ON A GAAP BASIS, BASED ON CURRENT SPOT RATES, THE COMPANY NOW EXPECTS A SLIGHT DECLINE IN GROSS MARGIN AND CONTINUE TO EXPECT A LOW-SINGLE-DIGIT DECLINE IN EARNINGS PER SHARE IN 2019.'}{'symbol': 'CTVA', 'date': '2019-10-31 22:30:00', 'title': 'CORTEVA, INC. PRESENTS AT MORGAN STANLEY GLOBAL CHEMICALS AND AGRICULTURE CONFERENCE, NOV-12-2019 08:45 AM', 'text': 'CORTEVA, INC. PRESENTS AT MORGAN STANLEY GLOBAL CHEMICALS AND AGRICULTURE CONFERENCE, NOV-12-2019 08:45 AM. VENUE: FOUR SEASONS HOTEL, BOSTON, MASSACHUSETTS, UNITED STATES. SPEAKERS: JAMES C. COLLINS, CEO & DIRECTOR.'}{'symbol': 'CTVA', 'date': '2019-10-31 13:30:00', 'title': 'CORTEVA SAYS LACK OF RAINFALL IS DELAYING SOYBEAN PLANTING IN BRAZIL - CONF CALL', 'text': 'CORTEVA SAYS LACK OF RAINFALL IS DELAYING SOYBEAN PLANTING IN BRAZIL, WHICH MAY HAVE AN IMPACT ON SECOND CROP - CONF CALL.CORTEVA SAYS EXPECT MORE NORMAL CONDITIONS TO ARRIVE IN MANY SECTORS OF THE AGRICULTURAL MARKETS IN 2020 - CONF CALL.CORTEVA SAYS IN NORT