INGS - CONVERSION OF ADJUSTED NET INCOME TO FREE CASH FLOW EXPECTED TO BE ABOUT 80% FOR FY 2019.GENERAC HOLDINGS - OPERATING AND FREE CASH FLOW GENERATION FOR THE FULL YEAR IS STILL EXPECTED TO BE STRONG FOR FY 2019.'}{'symbol': 'GILD', 'date': '2019-10-31 22:30:00', 'title': 'GILEAD AND GALAPAGOS TO PRESENT NEW DATA ON FILGOTINIB AT 2019 ACR/ARP ANNUAL MEETING', 'text': "GILEAD SCIENCES, INC. AND GALAPAGOS NV ANNOUNCED THAT NEW DATA FROM ACROSS THE COMPANIES' INFLAMMATORY DISEASE RESEARCH AND DEVELOPMENT PROGRAM WILL BE PRESENTED AT THE 2019 AMERICAN COLLEGE OF RHEUMATOLOGY/ASSOCIATION OF RHEUMATOLOGY PROFESSIONALS (ACR/ARP) ANNUAL MEETING IN ATLANTA FROM NOVEMBER 8-13. THE COMPANIES WILL PRESENT 20 ABSTRACTS AT THIS YEAR'S MEETING, INCLUDING KEY DATA ON THE INVESTIGATIONAL MEDICINE FILGOTINIB IN RHEUMATOID ARTHRITIS (RA) AND PSORIATIC ARTHRITIS (PSA), AS WELL AS REAL-WORLD RA TREATMENT OUTCOMES AND CARE. KEY PRESENTATIONS INCLUDE MULTIPLE SUBGROUP ANALYSES FROM THE FINCH 2 CLINICAL TRIAL THAT DEMONSTRATE THE POTENTIAL OF FILGOTINIB ACROSS SPECIFIC RA POPULATIONS WHO HAVE EXPERIENCED AN INADEQUATE RESPONSE TO BIOLOGIC DISEASE-MODIFYING ANTI-RHEUMATIC DRUGS (BDMARDS), INCLUDING THOSE IN THIS DIFFICULT-TO-TREAT POPULATION WITH ANEMIA, THROMBOCYTOPENIA AND LEUKOPENIA. KEY DATA WILL ALSO INCLUDE POOLED SAFETY RESULTS FROM THE PHASE 3 FINCH PROGRAM (NCT02889796, NCT02873936, NCT02886728), AND SAFETY OUTCOMES FROM THE LONG-TERM DARWIN-3 TRIAL (NCT02065700). A SUBGROUP ANALYSIS OF THE EFFICACY OF FILGOTINIB IN DEMOGRAPHIC AND CLINICAL SUBGROUPS OF PATIENTS WITH REFRACTORY RHEUMATOID ARTHRITIS (POSTER, #504, SUNDAY, NOV. 10; 9:00AM) A SUBGROUP ANALYSIS OF CLINICAL EFFICACY RESPONSE AND QUALITY OF LIFE OUTCOMES FROM PHASE 3 STUDY OF FILGOTINIB IN PATIENTS WITH INADEQUATE RESPONSE TO BIOLOGIC DMARDS (POSTER, #517, SUNDAY, NOV. 10; 9:00AM). IN RA, BIOMARKER RESEARCH SEEKS TO BETTER CHARACTERIZE THE MOLECULAR BASIS OF THE DISEASE AND IDENTIFY POPULATIONS THAT MAY BENEFIT MOST 